pytoy
=====

Copyright (c) 2026 Manfred Scheucher
Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

pytoy is an independent Python assembler, simulator, and GUI debugger for the
Toy CPU instruction set. Its code (assembler, GUI, CLI, C compiler) is original.

The Toy CPU instruction set (opcode values, the FETCH bit, and the execution
semantics) originates from the toycpu project by Jim Hall (FreeDOS Project):

    https://github.com/freedosproject/toycpu

toycpu is also MIT-licensed. Its original notice is reproduced below.

